# ioBroker.creality

Connects ioBroker to Creality Klipper-based printers (primarily **SPARKX i7**) via:

1. **Moonraker** HTTP API (default port `7125`, Fluidd often on `4408`) — print stats, temps, fans, CFS `box` object, G-code
2. **Creality WebSocket** (port `9999`) — toolhead light (`lightSw`), pause/resume (`pause`), stop (`stop`)

Prototype logic lives in `scripts/iobroker-print-status.js` until the adapter scaffold exists.

## Naming & scope

- Adapter name: **`iobroker.creality`** (not SPARKX-only, not “klipper-lite”)
- **Tested / primary target:** SPARKX i7 (+ CFS lite)
- Other Creality Klipper printers (K1/K2/Hi) may work partially; document as untested until confirmed
- Do **not** duplicate full `klipper-moonraker` object dump — keep a curated, VIS-friendly state tree

## Stack (match inventwo adapters)

- Plain **JavaScript** in `main.js` + `lib/` — no TypeScript build step; optional `npm run check`
- Admin UI via **jsonConfig** (`admin/jsonConfig.json`)
- HTTP: native `node:http` / `node:https` (no axios)
- WebSocket: Node built-in `WebSocket` (Node ≥ 22) or `ws` if needed
- Author / org: skvarel / inventwo (MIT)

## Git (mandatory)

- **Never** run `git commit`, `git push`, or releases unless the user explicitly asks
- User commits and pushes; releases via `npm run release-*` (AlCalzone release-script)
- **Never** run `npm run translate` — owner runs it manually before release

## Changelog & README (mandatory for every change)

Once the adapter scaffold exists, for **every code or config change** update `README.md`:

1. Add a user-facing entry under `### **WORK IN PROGRESS**` (English)
2. Format: `- (skvarel) Added|Fixed|Modified|… description` — no bold prefixes (`**FIXED**`, etc.)
3. Update Configuration / Data Points when options or states change
4. Do **not** edit `CHANGELOG_OLD.md` manually

Until scaffold exists, keep prototype changes documented briefly in chat / this folder’s TODO.

